      "id": 1,
      "text": "Moline was once called 'Dorr Centre' and was named after Thomas Wilson Dorr, a Rhode Island legislator who led the 1840s Dorr Rebellion.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dorr_Township%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Development was stimulated when the Grand Rapids and Indiana Railway came through in 1870 and established a station here.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dorr_Township%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The first permanent European‑American settlers in the township arrived in 1845.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
